Midlands Partnership University NHS Foundation Trust is seeking to identify providers able to deliver both an Electronic Prescribing and Medicines Administration (ePMA) system and an Electronic Prescription Service (EPS) capability, with implementation and go live anticipated from Financial Year 2028 onwards.

The Trust is seeking to engage with suitably qualified and experienced suppliers who may be able to provide an integrated solution covering both elements of the requirement.

The anticipated requirement is for a provider that can support the Trust with:
•	An Electronic Prescribing and Medicines Administration (ePMA) system; 
•	An Electronic Prescription Service (EPS) capability; 
•	Implementation, configuration, integration and associated technical services; 
•	Training, support and ongoing system maintenance; and 
•	Any associated services necessary to deliver a fully operational solution. 

The Trust is particularly interested in hearing from providers who can offer both the ePMA and EPS elements of the requirement, either through a single integrated solution or through an appropriate delivery model that provides the required functionality.

The Salvation Army invites suitably qualified and accredited organisations to tender for the provision of minibus driver training across the UK and Northern Ireland.

The Salvation Army operates approximately 52 minibuses, subject to change, which support a diverse range of services and locations. Drivers include officers, employees and volunteers, and passengers may include vulnerable individuals with differing mobility and support needs. 

The required service will include:
•	new-driver theory and practical training;
•	two-yearly refresher training;
•	accessible-minibus and wheelchair equipment training;
•	individual and group driver assessments;
•	passenger safety, safeguarding, first aid and emergency procedures;
•	certification of competent drivers;
•	reassessment arrangements where required; and
•	a live dashboard showing completed and forthcoming training. 
The successful provider must demonstrate national delivery capacity, recognised accreditation, appropriately qualified instructors, relevant multi-site delivery experience, appropriate insurance, robust safeguarding arrangements and valid Enhanced DBS checks for instructors.

Who Should Apply:
We invite expressions of interest from established training providers with proven experience.
